The 1957 Mafia meeting is spelled Apalachin (with one "p" and ending in "-in").
It is easy to confuse the two words because they look similar and share Native American roots, though they refer to completely different places and are pronounced differently:
• Apalachin (ap-uh-LAY-kin): A small hamlet in Tioga County in upstate New York, where the mob summit took place.
• Appalachian (ap-uh-LAY-shun or ap-uh-LATCH-un): The massive mountain range and cultural region stretching across the eastern United States from Alabama to Maine.
